  "interpretation": "Two separate questions, deliberately not conflated. (1) Applying our HVL estimator to TG-195's own distributed spectrum reproduces the HVL the report states, which validates the estimator. (2) Applying the same estimator to a SpekPy spectrum of the same nominal tube gives a harder/softer beam -- that residual is a difference between tube MODELS. TG-195 generated its spectra with the IPEM Report 78 software (report section 2.3, p.9); SpekPy implements a different model. The difference is not a defect in either, but it must not be absorbed silently: TG-195 gates use TG-195's distributed spectrum, and Phase-1b tunes filtration to a measured HVL, which makes the model choice second-order.",
